eight":3,"yt":"ERq5v_LcGWg","src":"musthear","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":235879004384475,"name":"RYM Top — Electronic — Electro-Industrial","rank":87,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":1}},{"id":45713649089455,"type":"album","name":"Echogenetic","artist":"Front Line Assembly","year":2013,"weight":3,"yt":"_Vz1PNW5P4M","src":"musthear","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":235879004384475,"name":"RYM Top — Electronic — Electro-Industrial","rank":179,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":1}},{"id":163278066396403,"type":"album","name":"Wake Up the Coma","artist":"Front Line Assembly","year":2019,"weight":3,"yt":"62cAntZEs1g","src":"musthear","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":123649763811663,"name":"RYM Top — Electronic — EBM","rank":179,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":1}}],"members":[],"member_of":[],"genres":[],"album_genres":[{"id":23184402430853,"type":"genre","name":"Electro-Industrial","n":12},{"id":107889004937350,"type":"genre","name":"EBM","n":8},{"id":87625349211221,"type":"genre","name":"electronic","n":4},{"id":15318882910861,"type":"genre","name":"Post-Industrial","n":3},{"id":274994627985231,"type":"genre","name":"Industrial","n":1},{"id":217093372136338,"type":"genre","name":"Industrial Metal","n":1},{"id":65067151178508,"type":"genre","name":"Electronic Dance Music","n":1}],"labels":[{"id":233179135397574,"type":"label","name":"Wax Trax!","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":21,"yt":null,"src":"ensayos"}],"album_labels":[],"own_scenes":[],"scenes":[{"id":61612725722255,"name":"Electronic Body Music","book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","start":1980,"end":1990,"desc":"Bélgica acuña una de las corrientes de baile industrial más exitosas, la «electronic body music», derivada del último Cabaret Voltaire con influencia disco y de ciencia ficción: Geography de Front 242 es el disco hito; después Klinik, Neon Judgement, Vomito Negro. En Vancouver, Skinny Puppy y Front Line Assembly, profetas de la generación cyberpunk. Los cimientos de la música de baile alternativa de los noventa.","color":"#94a3b8","family":"Gótico e industrial","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#ebm"},{"id":244014661214292,"name":"Industrial, EBM y The Final Cut","book":"Techno Rebels: The Renegades of Electronic Funk","author":"Dan Sicko","start":1981,"end":1991,"desc":"En 1989-1990 quien no escuchaba techno escuchaba industrial: Nitzer Ebb, Skinny Puppy, Front Line Assembly y los belgas Front 242 (Front by Front, 1988), con Chicago como centro americano (Ministry, Die Warzau, My Life with the Thrill Kill Kult, Wax Trax). Detroit tuvo su escena: Code Industry, el único grupo industrial enteramente afroamericano, y The Final Cut, de Jeff Mills y Tony Srock, banda de apoyo del grupo house True Faith (con Bridgett Grace) en Paragon, cuyo productor Jerry Capaldi acabó enfrentado a sus artistas y sembró desconfianza entre techno negro y blanco. Deep into the Cut (1990, Big Sex/Interfisch) cruzó EBM y techno; la última cita de Mills con ellos fue en el festival Atonal de Berlín. Srock los llevó hacia el rock (Consumed, Nettwerk, 1991).","color":"#a78bfa","family":"Raíces: Kraftwerk, electro, funk, italo y new wave","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/TechnoRebels/#industrial"},{"id":107889004937350,"name":"EBM","book":"Loops 1 y 2. Una historia de la música electrónica","author":"Javier Blánquez (ed.)","start":1981,"end":1990,"desc":"Colisión entre industrial y synth-pop: armazón rítmico marcial y bailable al servicio de canciones fronterizas con el rock duro (pero con máquinas).","color":"#94a3b8","family":"Industrial y ruido","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/loops_timeline/#ebm"}],"book_tracks":[{"id":153875290846640,"artist":"Front Line Assembly","artist_id":21942734857600,"title":"State Of Mind","year":1988,"ess":0,"yt":"lWOgIkQenSU","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Electronic Body Music","scene_id":61612725722255,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#ebm","chapters":["Sección 5.8"],"pages":[[1,141,null]]}],"mentions":[{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":141,"text":"…ghostly electronics, although they would reach a more cohesive sound on the concept VIVisectVI (1988) and on the Ministry-influenced Rabies (1989). Front Line Assembly (1) were also followers of Cabaret Voltaire and prophets of the cyber-punk generation. Their most refined recording was the technological poem State Of Mind (1988). Bill Leeb (whose real name is Wilhelm Schroeder) conducted at the same time a number of parallel projects: Cyberaktif, Noise Unit (Front Line Assembly's evil alter-ego), the progressive-house experiment Intermix, the ambient/new-age Delerium, Will and Synaestesia . The \"electronic body music\" of…"},{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":256,"text":"…Pitch Shifter were the main disciples of Godflesh's industrial-tinged grindcore. International EBM, 1992-98 EBM or \"electro\" (Cabaret Voltaire, Front Line Assembly, Skinny Puppy, Front 242) became more abrasive, brutal and visceral with Brainstorming (1992) by Germany's Yelworc (Domink van Reich), Solitary…"},{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":287,"text":"…system of the cyberpunk manifesto Soul of a New Machine (1992). Songs evolved rather than just erupt. The music of Demanufacture (1995), featuring Front Line Assembly's keyboardist Rhys Fulber, seemed to come from another world, saturated with blaspheme truths about this world. Its cascading bombshells kept…"},{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":297,"text":"…crafted Reflect Like A Mirror (1993), an impeccable follow-up to Brian Eno's and Harold Budd's classics. In Canada, Delerium (3), an offshoot of Front Line Assembly, crossed over into gothic, dance and pop music with meticulously and lushly arranged albums such as Stone Tower (1990), Spiritual Archives (1991)…"}],"podcast":[{"kind":"podcast","title":"Associated with Wax Trax","body":"Front Line Assembly was one of the bands associated with Wax Trax of Chicago, a specialist indie label for heavy music that appeared around 1990. \"This was the home of Ministry Front II IV II, Front Line Assembly and Dozens More.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The History of Indie Rock: Part 3","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sCtQqVBtCaI"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Presence in Industrial Scene","body":"Front Line Assembly was mentioned as one of the groups starting to gain notice within the rapidly growing industrial scene in the mid-to-late 1980s. \"Plus, people began to pick up on groups with names like Frontline Assembly, Pancao, Psychic TV, Liebach, and many others.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The Post-Punk Explosion Part 3: Industrial","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zSFhhEaiYwE"}]}],"awards":[],"concerts":[],"xref":[{"kind":"xref","title":"Associated with Wax Trax","body":"Ministry, fronted by Al Jourgensen, was one of the bands associated with Wax Trax of Chicago, a specialist indie label for heavy music that appeared around 1990. \"This was the home of Ministry Front II IV II, Front Line Assembly and Dozens More.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Ministry","from_id":8164776207386,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The History of Indie Rock: Part 3","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sCtQqVBtCaI"}]},{"kind":"xref","title":"Associated with Wax Trax","body":"Front 242 was one of the bands associated with Wax Trax of Chicago, a specialist indie label for heavy music that appeared around 1990. \"This was the home of Ministry Front II IV II, Front Line Assembly and Dozens More.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Front 242","from_id":137601747998064,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The History of Indie Rock: Part 3","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sCtQqVBtCaI"}]},{"kind":"xref","title":"Long-Running Project and Juno Awards","body":"Founded by Bill Leeb of the industrial band Front Line Assembly, Delirium has been an ongoing musical project since 1987, known for its \"transcendant stuff.\" The project has received two Juno Awards. \"Delirium has been an ongoing project since 1987, using guest appearances [...] And there have been two June Awards, too.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Delirium","from_id":116153175206740,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Where Are They Now? Part 4","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rrkmfJQBpHQ"}]}],"charts":[{"id":20956773886506,"type":"album","name":"The Initial Command","list_id":123649763811663,"list":"RYM Top — Electronic — EBM","src":"musthear","rank":124,"year":1987,"note":null,"yt":"g37ldnrIB_I","scaruffi":null},{"id":20956773886506,"type":"album","name":"The Initial Command","list_id":235879004384475,"list":"RYM Top — Electronic — Electro-Industrial","src":"musthear","rank":171,"year":1987,"note":null,"yt":"g37ldnrIB_I","scaruffi":null},{"id":965095988789,"type":"album","name":"Corrosion","list_id":123649763811663,"list":"RYM Top — Electronic — EBM","src":"musthear","rank":200,"year":1988,"note":null,"yt":"cGiNx5VL68Q","scaruffi":null},{"id":153875290846640,"type":"album","name":"State Of Mind","list_id":52032266791182,"list":"Scaruffi 1980s","src":"musthear","rank":431,"year":1988,"note":null,"yt":"lWOgIkQenSU","scaruffi":7.0},{"id":59744253295681,"type":"album","name":"Gashed Senses & Crossfire","list_id":123649763811663,"list":"RYM Top — Electronic — EBM","src":"musthear","rank":104,"year":1989,"note":null,"yt":"A1Ll1oEAnHo","scaruffi":null},{"id":59744253295681,"type":"album","name":"Gashed Senses & Crossfire","list_